# Secrets. The form endpoint reads its keys from the environment and
# nothing else — RESEND_API_KEY, WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY, INQUIRY_TO — and
# those live in the host's settings, never here. This is belt and braces
# for a local .env someone makes while testing.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Client-confidential source material — must never reach the public repo
# or a published URL. See netlify-build.sh for the publish allow-list.
*.docx
Cuddle Avenue Assets/
assets/img/_source/
dist/

# Camera originals dropped in for processing — 775 MB of HEIC/JPG/MOV that
# no browser can serve as-is. Only the optimised derivatives belong in the
# repo (assets/img/, assets/video/), never these.
assets/Pictures & Video_s/
assets/Programs/
assets/Menu Pictures/

# Licensed stock originals (45 MB of full-resolution Adobe Stock). The
# cropped derivatives in assets/img/stock-*.jpg|webp are what ships; the
# licence IDs are recorded in BRIEF-COMPLIANCE.md.
assets/AdobeStock_*.jpeg

# Client material dropped in the project root: Ayna's design mockups, PDFs,
# review exports and question lists. Working references, not site source;
# the published handbook lives in assets/docs/.
/*.png
/*.pdf
/*reviews.txt
/CLIENT-QUESTIONS.md
/Enrichment/
/New folder/
/Pictures under the hero/
/montage
/Pics reupload/
